"[2310.09443] G10: Enabling An Efficient Unified GPU Memory and Storage Architecture with Smart Tensor Migrations (https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.09443)\nciteturn11view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.09443\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Hardware Architecture\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 13 Oct 2023]\nL9: # Title:G10: Enabling An Efficient Unified GPU Memory and Storage Architecture with Smart Tensor Migrations\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Haoyang Zhang】, 【6†Yirui Eric Zhou】, 【7†Yuqi Xue】, 【8†Yiqi Liu】, 【9†Jian Huang】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled G10: Enabling An Efficient Unified GPU Memory and Storage Architecture with Smart Tensor Migrations, by Haoyang Zhang and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【10†View PDF】 【11†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:To break the GPU memory wall for scaling deep learning workloads, a variety of architecture and system techniques have been proposed recently. Their typical approaches include memory extension with flash memory and direct storage access. However, these techniques still suffer from suboptimal performance and introduce complexity to the GPU memory management, making them hard to meet the scalability requirement of deep learning workloads today.\nL17: In this paper, we present a unified GPU memory and storage architecture named G10 driven by the fact that the tensor behaviors of deep learning workloads are highly predictable. G10 integrates the host memory, GPU memory, and flash memory into a unified memory space, to scale the GPU memory capacity while enabling transparent data migrations. Based on this unified GPU memory and storage architecture, G10 utilizes compiler techniques to characterize the tensor behaviors in deep learning workloads.\nL18: Therefore, it can schedule data migrations in advance by considering the available bandwidth of flash memory and host memory. The cooperative mechanism between deep learning compilers and the unified memory architecture enables G10 to hide data transfer overheads in a transparent manner. We implement G10 based on an open-source GPU simulator. Our experiments demonstrate that G10 outperforms state-of-the-art GPU memory solutions by up to 1.75$\\times$, without code modifications to deep learning workloads.\nL19: With the smart data migration mechanism, G10 can reach 90.3\\% of the performance of the ideal case assuming unlimited GPU memory.\nL20: Comments:  | This paper is accepted at The 56th IEEE/ACM International Symposium on Microarchitecture (MICRO'23). *Co-primary authors\nL21: Subjects:  | Hardware Architecture (cs.AR); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL22: Cite as:  | 【12†arXiv:2310.09443】 [cs.AR]\nL23:    | (or 【13†arXiv:2310.09443v1】 [cs.AR] for this version)\nL24:    | 【14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2310.09443†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | 【15†https://doi.org/10.1145/3613424.3614309†doi.org】 DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Haoyang Zhang [【16†view email】]\nL29: [v1] Fri, 13 Oct 2023 23:32:28 UTC (3,287 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled G10: Enabling An Efficient Unified GPU Memory and Storage Architecture with Smart Tensor Migrations, by Haoyang Zhang and 4 other authors\nL36: \nL37:   * 【10†View PDF】\nL38:   * 【11†HTML (experimental)】\nL39:   * 【17†TeX Source】\nL40: \nL41: 【18†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.AR\nL45: \nL46: 【19†< prev】   |   【20†next >】\nL47: \nL48: 【21†new】 | 【22†recent】 | 【23†2023-10】\nL49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: 【24†cs】\nL53: 【2